frame(y = [0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1], a = [1.0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], b = [1.0, 1, 2, 5, 6, 6]).glm(y ~ a + b, family: binomial)
---
error[Z0803]: glm: `a` and `b` each perfectly predict `y` (separation)
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:83
  |
1 | frame(y = [0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1], a = [1.0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], b = [1.0, 1, 2, 5, 6, 6]).glm(y ~ a + b, family: binomial)
  |                                                                                   ^^^ estimates diverge; maximum likelihood does not exist
  |
